  "labelled": [
    {
      "task": "TASK-116",
      "criterion": "TASK-AC-85F76FF493AB",
      "text": "`askCompletion`: a For Time with no cap is not asked \"Work completed\"; a For Time's amounts belong to a race answered Incomplete, never to one nobody answered."
    },
    {
      "task": "TASK-116",
      "criterion": "AC-R010-01",
      "text": "For Time starts where the race ended and keeps only the athlete's answer (`workCompleted`); with no cap nothing is asked or claimed."
    },
    {
      "task": "TASK-116",
      "criterion": "TASK-AC-8FF68F3F5241",
      "text": "AMRAP and For Time save authority: a refused save is kept on the attempt's record and said after a reload; a known row whose richer save failed reopens the block."
    },
    {
      "task": "TASK-117",
      "criterion": "AC-R015-01",
      "text": "An AMRAP asks no per-movement amount until a rounds count is recorded (TASK-015, `partialRoundFor`), so the amrap state's log past its cap draws only the loaded kb swing's \"Weight used\" group (bec4454 drew \"Completed in next round\" for every movement); a recorded count draws each movement's next-round amount, and a changed count clears the amounts and keeps the loads. Labels stay Round 7's."
    },
    {
      "task": "TASK-117",
      "criterion": "AC-C37-01",
      "text": "A load field only where a load can attach (`loadApplies`, the set logger's rule the saved row also applies); a multi-round For Time asks loads only; a distance amount takes decimals; the row's own rule (`movementActualFromDraft`) says in the field what an entry is refused on. No accepted state draws a refusal, a distance or a multi-round race, and every accepted state's loaded movement keeps its load field."
    },
    {
      "task": "TASK-117",
      "criterion": "TASK-AC-FB8AF4D9B641",
      "text": "AC-C26-01's exact per-movement group list (a group only for the loaded movement before rounds are recorded) is the drawing above; the form keeps its accepted name \"Log section results\" (R7-3)."
    },
    {
      "task": "TASK-117",
      "criterion": "AC-R011-01",
      "text": "An EMOM's clock caption says \"· Rest\" beside its minute while the block's own rest window runs. The accepted emom state prescribes no rest, so it draws no change."
    },
    {
      "task": "TASK-117",
      "criterion": "TASK-AC-8C147E2C148D",
      "text": "The card's \"Log results\" action states whether its dialog is open (`aria-expanded`); nothing drawn changes."
    },
    {
      "task": "TASK-117",
      "criterion": "TASK-AC-339D1096F660",
      "text": "Each movement's typed amount and load are kept on the attempt's own record (EMOM, AMRAP, For Time) and restored after a reload; the gallery keeps nothing, so it draws no change."
    },
    {
      "task": "TASK-117",
      "criterion": "TASK-AC-D58939F8E091",
      "text": "EMOM save authority, as the AMRAP's and For Time's: a refused save is kept on the EMOM's record and said after a reload; a known row whose richer save failed reopens the block. Nothing the gallery draws changes."
    }
  ],
  "unintended": []
